          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पतति (patati) — \"(he, she, it) falls\". A leaf, a पत्रम्, पतति."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Patati is the present of the root √pat, which first meant \"to fly\" and then \"to fall\" (CDIAL 7722). It is inherited: MW compares Greek petomai, \"I fly\". It lives on as Hindi paṛnā, \"to fall\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What leaves and rain do."
